{"id":"sh/jqpwzq54","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":263,"width":1136,"height":92},"text":"Enter an object name or sky position. Explore a sequence of SPHEREx observations, then explain what the images support.","style":{"fontSize":31,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/z6hc3mxs","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":387,"width":553,"height":37},"text":"The learner’s question","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/yl8vahg7","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":432,"width":553,"height":156},"text":"A student sees a star shift between two images. Is it motion, a different infrared wavelength, or an unreliable pixel? Dates and quality information help the student test that first impression.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/l8ze5wfy","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":387,"width":561,"height":37},"text":"Our contribution","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/k7qdcryd","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":432,"width":561,"height":156},"text":"A public time-sequence viewer, three guided investigations and a portable evidence notebook. The learner’s explanation stays attached to the observations and exact archive sources that support it.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
